{"id":"housing-timelines-by-year","title":"San Francisco's housing timelines, year by year","question":"Each year, how long did San Francisco's reported housing projects take at each stage, and where did the city rank among the nine?","finding":"San Francisco was the slowest of the cities with enough linked projects in 5 of 7 years for application to entitlement, 5 of 7 for entitlement to permit and 1 of 8 for permit to completion. In 2025 its medians were 304 days, 266 days and 645 days. The city reported 4,034 homes completed in 2018 and 2,844 in 2025.","how":"The same joins as the city table, grouped by the year in which the later date falls. A median is shown only with at least 5 linked projects; the rank counts only cities with a median that year (1 is slowest). \"Other cities\" is the middle value of the other cities' medians.","limits":"Few San Francisco projects can be linked from entitlement to permit in any one year, so those medians move a lot. A year's figure reflects projects finishing that stage in that year, some of which started many years earlier; the first report years understate, because both dates must fall inside the reporting period to be linked. The limits listed for the city table apply here too.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"year","t":"Report year","type":"year"},{"k":"appToEnt","t":"Application to entitlement, days","type":"int"},{"k":"appToEntOthers","t":"Other cities","type":"int"},{"k":"appToEntRank","t":"Rank (1 slowest)","type":"text"},{"k":"entToPermit","t":"Entitlement to permit, days","type":"int"},{"k":"entToPermitN","t":"Projects linked","type":"int"},{"k":"entToPermitOthers","t":"Other cities","type":"int"},{"k":"entToPermitRank","t":"Rank (1 slowest)","type":"text"},{"k":"permitToDone","t":"Permit to completion, days","type":"int"},{"k":"permitToDoneOthers","t":"Other cities","type":"int"},{"k":"permitToDoneRank","t":"Rank (1 slowest)","type":"text"},{"k":"entitled","t":"Homes entitled","type":"int"},{"k":"permitted","t":"H